id: pm-pwqiao
title: "files/docs --add refusal does not name the note segment it misread as a key, nor offer the standalone --note flag"
description: "Found 2026-11-10 while linking evidence for pm-5htunt. 'pm files <id> --add \"path=a.txt,scope=project,note=Single-label host, host:port, whitespace\"' exits with invalid_argument and the message says only 'Expected key=value entries separated by commas'. Cause (src/core/item/parse.ts parseCsvKv; corrected after review on PR 1701): after a comma, the identifier-shaped segment 'host:port' opens a new markdown-style key 'host' (the pm-fr10t8 / GH-258 boundary keeps identifier-shaped keys strict). The next segment ' whitespace' has no delimiter, and 'host' is not a continuable key, so parseCsvKv throws the generic invalid-entry refusal; the unknown-key check (assertNoUnknownCsvKeys) is never reached. If the note ends with 'host:port' instead, the entry reaches the unknown-key refusal. Commas alone are accepted as note continuation ('a, b and c'), so an agent cannot tell from either refusal which segment broke the entry. Neither refusal mentions the standalone --note flag (pm-pfnx, GH-170), which takes free text with no parsing. Reproduced with the built CLI in a sandbox tracker. Duplicate check: searched 'files --add note colon comma csv key value parse'; pm-fr10t8 (closed) fixed non-identifier candidate keys and deliberately keeps the identifier case strict; pm-0v9k (closed) introduced strict rejection."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: agent-ux,files,parser,recovery
created_at: "2026-11-10T14:07:56.498Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T08:42:37.974Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-11T08:02:13.936Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-11T08:02:13.936Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "A files/docs --add refusal caused by an unknown key from a continuation segment names that segment and key in details and in the message; The recovery offers the same link with the prose moved to the standalone --note flag (or a quoting form the parser accepts), and executing it links the file with the full note text; GH-258 strict rejection of identifier-shaped typo keys such as lable=main is unchanged; Both refusal paths are covered, with tests for each variant: the generic invalid-entry refusal raised in parseCsvKv when a later segment follows a non-continuable key (the recorded example), and the unknown-key refusal when the note ends with the key-shaped segment (note=... host:port)"
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "parseAddEntriesWithNoteRecovery in src/sdk/linked-artifacts.ts rethrows a note-caused refusal as linked_artifact_note_key_misread. The message and details name misread_segment, misread_key, note and the underlying cause. recovery.suggested_retry_args holds the single-entry link with --note plus the invocation's scope and controls. Other refusals, including GH-258 typo keys, keep their own messages."
expected_result: The refusal names the misread note segment and offers an executable --note retry that links the full note
actual_result: "All three variants (generic, unknown-key, repeated-key) name the segment, and executing the emitted retry links a.txt with the full note text"
