comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-11T08:42:37.973Z","harness:claude-code","PR 1705 review round 1 (Greptile P1 and Codex P2), fixed. The recovery used to rebuild one entry with a regex, which broke in two cases. A quoted path such as path=\"a,note=literal.txt\" was matched inside the quotes. A later link key such as scope=global was folded into the note. The retry also dropped --migrate, --remove and --add-glob. findMisreadNoteSegment now reads the entry with splitStructuredEntrySegments (src/core/item/parse.ts), which uses parseCsvKv's own quote and escape rules. Link keys before the note, and a non-repeated path or scope after it, stay link fields; every other later segment is note prose. The entry is rewritten with the note JSON-quoted (note=\"...\"). The retry replays the whole invocation from the resolved values: every --add, --add-glob, --remove, --migrate, --note, --append-stable, --validate-paths, --full-history, --author, --message and --force. Executing it was proven for the migration and removal case, a quoted path, a later scope key, embedded quotes and a URL in the prose."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-11T06:43:25.190Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation on branch fix/collection-mutation-receipts (2026-11-11). runLinkedArtifacts parses --add entries through parseAddEntriesWithNoteRecovery. When parsing refuses, the first failing entry is located and findMisreadNoteSegment is asked three questions:\n- Does the entry carry note= or note: ?\n- Does a later comma segment open with an identifier followed by = or : (URLs excluded)?\n- Does the link alone, the text before note, parse cleanly?\n\nOnly then is the refusal rethrown as linked_artifact_note_key_misread. The message names the segment and key, and details carries entry_index, misread_segment, misread_key, note and cause. recovery.suggested_retry_args and nextSteps hold the same link with the prose moved to --note; --note takes it verbatim, and the retry is rendered with resolvePmCommandScopeArgs. The retry also carries --append-stable (files only), --author, --message and --force. required says that other entries of a refused multi-entry invocation were not written.\n\nEvery other refusal keeps its message: a typo key with no note (GH-258 lable=main), or an invalid link such as scope=bogus.\n\nEvidence. Executing the emitted retry against a sandbox tracker links a.txt with the full note text in all three variants:\n- the generic invalid-entry refusal ('host:port, whitespace');\n- the unknown-key refusal (note ending 'host:port');\n- the repeated-key refusal from pm-oglm0t ('path: b.txt').\n\nSpecs: tests/unit/sdk/linked-artifact-note-recovery.spec.ts."
